==Serbo-Croatian==
{{wikipedia|lang=sh}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bêoɡrad/|lang=sh}}
* {{hyphenation|Be|o|grad}}
* {{audio|Sr-beograd.ogg|audio}}

===Etymology===
Composed of [[Ekavian]] Serbo-Croatian {{term/t|sh|bȅo||white}} (from {{etyl|sla-pro|sh}} {{term/t|sla-pro|*bělъ}}) and {{term/t|sh|grȃd||city}} (from {{etyl|sla-pro|sh}} {{term/t|sla-pro|*gordъ}}). The city is named after the white wall of the fortress that enclosed the city. See also {{term|Biograd|lang=sh}}, {{term|Бе́лгород|tr=Bélgorod|sc=Cyrl|lang=ru}}, {{term|Białogard}}.

===Proper noun===
{{sh-proper noun|g=m|head=Bȅograd|r|Београд|Бе̏оград}}

